Careful: '2×3' multiplication sign fine.

Status all 'rencana'.

Now src/lib/tools.ts:

```ts
import type { ToolMeta, ToolCategory } from './tool-types';
import { categories } from './tool-types';

const modules = import.meta.glob<{ meta: ToolMeta }>('../features/*/meta.ts', { eager: true });

const categoryOrder = new Map(categories.map((c, i) => [c.id, i]));

export const tools: ToolMeta[] = Object.values(modules)
  .map((mod) => mod.meta)
  .sort((a, b) => (categoryOrder.get(a.category) ?? 99) - (categoryOrder.get(b.category) ?? 99) || a.name.localeCompare(b.name, 'id'));

export function getTool(slug: string): ToolMeta | undefined {
  return tools.find((t) => t.slug === slug);
}

export function relatedTools(tool: ToolMeta, count = 3): ToolMeta[] {
  const sameCategory = tools.filter((t) => t.slug !== tool.slug && t.category === tool.category);
  const others = tools.filter((t) => t.slug !== tool.slug && t.category !== tool.category);
  return [...sameCategory, ...others].slice(0, count);
}
```
import.meta.glob typing in Astro/TS may need `vite/client` types. tsconfig? Let me check tsconfig later; Astro generates .astro/types and includes astro/client which defines ImportMeta.glob? Astro's tsconfig `astro/tsconfigs/base` includes. Current tsconfig unknown (109 bytes). Might fail `astro check`. Fallback: explicit imports in tools.ts (6 imports) — simpler, deterministic, no glob typing issues, and still "registry driven by meta.ts". But PRD says catalog built automatically from meta.ts so adding a tool doesn't change homepage code. Explicit imports in one registry file also means adding tool = add import (still no homepage change). Glob is more faithful.

Let me check tsconfig and whether ImportMeta.glob types resolve. I'll write with glob and run check; if it errors, switch.

Actually simpler & robust: use glob with `as unknown as Record<string, {meta: ToolMeta}>`? Let me first try, then check.

search.ts:
```ts
export function normalize(value: string): string {
  return value.toLowerCase().normalize('NFD').replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g, '');
}

export function matches(haystack: string[], query: string): boolean {
  const q = normalize(query).trim();
  if (!q) return true;
  const words = q.split(/\s+/);
  return words.every((word) => haystack.some((h) => normalize(h).includes(word)));
}

export function searchText(tool) { return [tool.name, tool.category, ...tool.keywords, tool.tagline] }
```
But importing tool-types type only; fine. Put searchText in tool-types? Let's put in search.ts with ToolMeta type import.

Now components. Let me write Icon.astro.

Paths (Lucide 24x24, stroke 1.75, round caps):
- search: `<circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m20 20-3.5-3.5"/>`
- sun: `<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4"/>`
