- laptop (lokal): `<rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="12" rx="2"/><path d="M2 19h20"/>`
- server (server): `<rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="3" y="13" width="18" height="7" rx="2"/><path d="M7 7.5h.01M7 16.5h.01"/>`
- pencil (draw): `<path d="M12 20h9"/><path d="M16.5 3.5a2.1 2.1 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4Z"/>`
- network (diagram): `<rect x="9" y="3" width="6" height="5" rx="1"/><rect x="3" y="16" width="6" height="5" rx="1"/><rect x="15" y="16" width="6" height="5" rx="1"/><path d="M12 8v4M6 16v-2h12v2"/>`
- file-text (pdf): `<path d="M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8Z"/><path d="M14 3v5h5M9 13h6M9 17h6"/>`
- user-round (photo): `<circle cx="12" cy="9" r="3.5"/><path d="M5.5 20a6.5 6.5 0 0 1 13 0"/>`
- link (share): `<path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7 0l2-2a5 5 0 0 0-7-7l-1 1"/><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7 0l-2 2a5 5 0 0 0 7 7l1-1"/>`
- braces (generator): `<path d="M8 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2 2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h1"/><path d="M16 3h1a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2 2 2 0 0 0-2 2v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-1"/>`
- x (close): `<path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/>`
- arrow-left? skip.
- corner-down-left (enter hint): skip.

Icon component:
```astro
---
interface Props { name: IconName; size?: number; class?: string }
---
<svg ... aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width={size} height={size} viewBox="0 0 24 24">{...}</svg>
```
Astro doesn't allow `{...}` switch inside easily; use a map of path strings and use set:html. Better: define `const paths: Record<IconName,string>` with raw HTML and `<Fragment set:html={paths[name]} />` inside svg. Works.

Alternatively a component per icon; too many files. Use map + set:html. Since content is static source, safe.

Now Button.astro:
```astro
---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
type Variant = 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'ghost' | 'danger';
interface Props {
  variant?: Variant;
  href?: string;
  type?: 'button' | 'submit' | 'reset';
  disabled?: boolean;
  loading?: boolean;
  class?: string;
}
const { variant='secondary', href, type='button', disabled=false, loading=false, class: className } = Astro.props;
const cls = ['btn', `btn--${variant}`, className].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
---
{href ? <a href={href} class={cls}><slot /></a> : <button type={type} class={cls} disabled={disabled || loading}><slot /></button>}
```
Loading state: spinner + text; keep simple: if loading, add aria-busy and a spinner span. Unused currently.

Careful with disabled attribute on button: `disabled={disabled || loading}` renders when false? Astro omits false attributes for boolean. Fine.

Input.astro:
```astro
---
interface Props {
  id: string; label: string; type?: string; name?: string; placeholder?: string; value?: string;
  hint?: string; error?: string; required?: boolean; autocomplete?: string; class?: string; list?: string;
}
const { id, label, type='text', name, placeholder, value, hint, error, required, autocomplete, class: className } = Astro.props;
const describedBy = [hint ? `${id}-hint` : null, error ? `${id}-error` : null].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
---
<div class={className}>
  <label class="field-label" for={id}>{label}{required && <span aria-hidden="true"> *</span>}</label>
  <input id={id} ... aria-invalid={error ? 'true':'undefined'} aria-describedby={describedBy || undefined} />
  {hint && <p class="field-hint" id={`${id}-hint`}>{hint}</p>}
  {error && <p class="field-error" id={`${id}-error`}><Icon name="alert" size={16} />{error}</p>}
</div>
```
Need an alert icon. Add 'alert' path: circle + line. Also required indicator needs screen-reader text not just *: use `<span aria-hidden="true"> *</span>` plus sr-only "wajib diisi". Let's do `<span class="sr-only"> (wajib)</span><span aria-hidden="true"> *</span>`.

Dropzone.astro:
```astro
---
interface Props { id: string; label: string; accept?: string; multiple?: boolean; maxSize?: string; hint?: string; }
---
<div class="dropzone" data-dropzone>
  <Icon name="upload" size={24} />
  <p>{label}</p>
  <input id={id} type="file" class="sr-only" accept={accept} multiple={multiple} />
  <label class="btn btn--secondary" for={id}>Pilih file</label>
  {hint && <p class="field-hint">{hint}</p>}
  <p class="field-hint" data-dropzone-file hidden></p>
</div>
<script>...</script>
