```ts
const dialog = document.getElementById('palette') as HTMLDialogElement | null;
if (dialog) {
  const input = dialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-palette-input]');
  const items = Array.from(dialog.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-palette-item]'));
  const empty = dialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-palette-empty]');

  const visibleLinks = () => items.filter(i => !i.hidden).map(i => i.querySelector('a')).filter((a): a is HTMLAnchorElement => Boolean(a));

  const filter = () => {
    const query = input?.value ?? '';
    let shown = 0;
    items.forEach(item => {
      const ok = matches([item.dataset.search ?? ''], query);
      item.hidden = !ok;
      if (ok) shown++;
    });
    if (empty) empty.hidden = shown !== 0;
  };

  const open = () => {
    if (dialog.open) return;
    if (input) input.value = '';
    filter();
    dialog.showModal();
    input?.focus();
  };

  document.querySelectorAll('[data-open-palette]').forEach(trigger => trigger.addEventListener('click', open));

  document.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
    const target = event.target as HTMLElement | null;
    const typing = target && (target.tagName === 'INPUT' || target.tagName === 'TEXTAREA' || target.isContentEditable);
    if ((event.ctrlKey || event.metaKey) && event.key.toLowerCase() === 'k') {
      event.preventDefault();
      dialog.open ? dialog.close() : open();
      return;
    }
    if (event.key === '/' && !typing && !dialog.open) {
      event.preventDefault();
      open();
    }
  });

  input?.addEventListener('input', filter);

  input?.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
    if (event.key === 'ArrowDown' || event.key === 'ArrowUp') {
      event.preventDefault();
      const links = visibleLinks();
      if (links.length === 0) return;
      const index = event.key === 'ArrowDown' ? 0 : links.length - 1;
      links[index]?.focus();
    }
  });

  dialog.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
    const links = visibleLinks();
    const current = links.indexOf(document.activeElement as HTMLAnchorElement);
    if (current === -1) return;
    if (event.key === 'ArrowDown') {
      event.preventDefault();
      links[(current + 1) % links.length]?.focus();
    }
    if (event.key === 'ArrowUp') {
      event.preventDefault();
      links[(current - 1 + links.length) % links.length]?.focus();
    }
  });
}
```
Note: filter uses matches([...]) where dataset.search already normalized haystack joined. matches normalizes again, fine.

Escape: native closes dialog. After close, focus returns to trigger (native behavior restores focus to previously focused element). Good.

But when opened via Ctrl+K, previously focused element restored — fine.

`dialog.open ? dialog.close() : open()` — dialog.close() returns focus.

One catch: `<dialog>` closes on Escape by default; also need to ensure clicking backdrop works (Modal script handles).

Since CommandPalette renders Modal, and Modal's script runs querySelectorAll('dialog.modal') — ordering: Modal's script is separate module; both run. Fine.

Now the palette dialog label: aria-labelledby="palette-title" pointing to visible label element.

Write Header with scoped style for header-link.

Header markup: search-trigger needs mobile icon-only. I'll write CSS in global (edit) rather than scoped. Let me instead put the search trigger styles in Header scoped <style> to avoid editing global much. But .search-trigger already in global with display:none. I'll edit global's search-trigger block.

Let me do edits to global.css after writing components.

Plan the edits:
1. Replace `.search-trigger { display:none; ... }` block with mobile-friendly version.
2. Remove `@media (min-width:768px){ .search-trigger { display:inline-flex; } }` block.
3. Add `.header-link` style.

I'll rewrite those sections with edit tool.

Now writing components.

