</script>

content.text:
Now the JSON pane.

Layout: two panes. Input pane head with title "Input" + Format/Minify. Output pane head with title "Hasil" + segmented + Salin.

Icons: alert for error.

Input textarea with `aria-describedby="json-error"`? Only when error exists. Set dynamically in JS: `input.setAttribute('aria-invalid','true')` and `aria-describedby="json-error-text"`. Fine.

Sample button in empty state:
```astro
<div class="preview-empty" id="json-empty">
	<p>Tempel JSON di kiri, hasilnya muncul di sini.</p>
	<button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary mt-3" id="json-sample">Isi contoh</button>
</div>
```
Wait, `.preview-empty` is a `<p>` class usually. Here a div. Style `.preview-empty { }` applies. But hidden toggling.

Hmm, `mt-3` is a Tailwind utility; project uses Tailwind v4 so `mt-3` works (stage 1 used `mt-4` in empty state). Fine.

JSON output: `<pre class="code-block" id="json-output" hidden><code id="json-output-code"></code></pre>` — `.code-block` should have padding and mono. But it's inside a pane with rounded corners.

Tree wrapper: `<div class="json-tree-wrap" id="json-tree" hidden></div>`.

Script:
```ts
import { copyText } from '../../lib/clipboard';
import { formatJson, highlightJson, minifyJson, renderJsonTree, type JsonError } from '../../lib/json-tools';
import { toast } from '../../lib/toast';

const input = ...;
...
let currentText = '';
let view: 'teks' | 'pohon' = 'teks';

const setEmpty = (blank: boolean) => { empty.hidden = !blank; output.hidden = blank || view !== 'teks'; tree.hidden = blank || view !== 'pohon'; };

const showError = (error: JsonError) => {
	errorText.textContent = `Baris ${error.line}, kolom ${error.column}: ${error.message}`;
	errorBox.hidden = false;
	input.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true');
	input.setAttribute('aria-describedby', 'json-error-text');
	input.focus();
	const start = Math.min(error.index, input.value.length);
	input.setSelectionRange(start, start);
};

const clearError = () => {
	errorBox.hidden = true;
	input.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');
	input.removeAttribute('aria-describedby');
	errorText.textContent = '';
};
```
Note: selecting zero-length at error index. Fine.

Format:
```ts
const run = (mode: 'format' | 'minify') => {
	clearError();
	const result = mode === 'format' ? formatJson(input.value) : minifyJson(input.value);
	if (!result.ok) {
		currentText = '';
		outputCode.textContent = '';
		tree.innerHTML = '';
		copy.disabled = true;
		setEmpty(true);
		showError(result.error);
		return;
	}
	currentText = result.text;
	outputCode.innerHTML = highlightJson(result.text);
	tree.innerHTML = renderJsonTree(result.data, { openDepth: 1 });
	copy.disabled = false;
	setEmpty(false);
};

const setView = (next: 'teks' | 'pohon') => {
	view = next;
	viewButtons.forEach(b => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', b.dataset.view === next ? 'true' : 'false'));
	setEmpty(currentText === '');
};
```
`setEmpty` uses `view`; define with the parameter blank.

Actually simpler:
```ts
const paint = () => {
	const blank = currentText === '';
	empty.hidden = !blank;
	output.hidden = blank || view !== 'teks';
	tree.hidden = blank || view !== 'pohon';
};
```

On input: currentText=''; clearError(); outputCode.textContent=''; tree.innerHTML=''; copy.disabled=true; paint().

Sample:
```ts
sample.addEventListener('click', () => {
	input.value = '{\n  "proyek": "toolsman",\n  "alat": 6,\n  "gratis": true\n}';
	input.focus();
	run('format');
});
```
Placeholder JSON uses single quotes in Astro attribute with escaped quotes: `placeholder='{"proyek": "toolsman", "alat": 6}'`.

Careful: Astro attribute with single quotes containing double quotes is fine.

Now tool.astro with Tabs.

Then tools.ts + ToolPage.

