```

Replace with shareEnv.

Also `env!` usages. Let me rewrite the frontmatter section to be cleaner with a local `env` variable.

New:
```ts
const loaded = shareEnv();
const valid = ID_PATTERN.test(id) && loaded !== null;
const row = valid ? await loaded!.DB... : null;
```
Hmm `loaded` narrowing across await isn't automatic but `loaded!` works.

Cleaner:
```ts
const env = ID_PATTERN.test(id) ? shareEnv() : null;
const row = env ? await env.DB.prepare(...)... : null;
const view = viewShare(row, Date.now());
const files = env && view.state === 'ok' ? ... : [];
```
Note: if env is null, viewShare(null) → missing. Good, no need for the ternary on view.

